Saturate out-of-range coordinates in splashFloor()/splashCeil().

Device coordinates outside the int range (e.g. a stroke under
"1 1000000 0 792 1 3 cm") reach splashFloor()/splashCeil(), whose generic
implementations then do an undefined double -> int conversion (UBSan:
"SplashMath.h:78:29: runtime error: -4.85405e+11 is outside the range of
representable values of type 'int'", from Splash::pathAllOutside() <
fillWithPattern() < strokeWide()). x86-64 yields INT_MIN, wasm saturates.
Saturate explicitly (NaN -> INT_MIN). With INT_MAX now possible on every host,
also keep the "+ 1" in SplashClip::testRect()/testSpan() and in
SplashXPathScanner::addIntersection() from overflowing, and return early from
Splash::drawSpan() when clipping leaves an empty span, instead of computing a
pipe position for an out-of-range x0 (Splash.cc:1288 "4 * 2147483647").

No regression test: no input found that fails without the fix other than
under UBSan. x86-64 converts out-of-range doubles to INT_MIN and wasm32
saturates, and the repro renders without a fault in the unfixed wasm32 builds
of all four fuzz targets; a native ASan+UBSan build reports only the
SplashMath.h conversion above (poppler-pdf, poppler-page_search). The patch
removes undefined behaviour on these paths.

Not fixed upstream as of 9182fd5.
Upstream: open umbrella issue poppler/poppler#1764 (by LingMaple, 2026-07-20) covers float-to-int overflows from untrusted doubles; it lists other sites, not Splash::drawSpan or SplashClip::testRect/testSpan.

